title: Documentation
views:
  - path: frigate-docs
    title: Frigate
    icon: mdi:cctv
    theme: default
    badges: []
    cards:
      - type: markdown
        title: Frigate - simple explanation
        content: |
          # Frigate

          Frigate is the “camera brain” in this setup.
          It watches the video from your cameras and tries to understand what it sees.

          In simple words:
          - it notices movement
          - it tries to identify what it is
          - it tells Home Assistant what happened
          - Home Assistant can then decide what to do

          This is useful when you want the house to react to people, animals, or faces.

      - type: markdown
        title: Easy version
        content: |
          ## What Frigate does in everyday language

          Think of Frigate like a smart security helper.

          It can:
          - detect a person
          - detect an animal
          - detect a face
          - notice when something happens in a certain area, such as the backyard or driveway
          - send information to your Home Assistant automations

          When it sees something important, your home can react.
          For example:
          - turn on lights
          - send a phone notification
          - start a siren
          - blink lights inside to get attention

      - type: markdown
        title: How it works
        content: |
          ## A simple example

          1. A camera sees movement.
          2. Frigate looks at the image.
          3. It tries to decide if it is a person, animal, or face.
          4. It sends that information to Home Assistant.
          5. Home Assistant checks the rules and decides what should happen.

          Example:
          - a person appears at the back of the house at night
          - Frigate recognizes it as a person
          - the lights turn on
          - you get a notification

      - type: markdown
        title: More advanced version
        content: |
          ## How the logic works in more detail

          The Frigate package is not only “detect something”.
          It also checks conditions before acting.

          ### Important ideas

          - Trigger: what starts the process
          - Condition: what must be true before the action runs
          - Action: what the house actually does

          In this setup, the system often checks things like:
          - which camera saw the event
          - whether the event is in a special zone such as “Baksidan”
          - whether you are home, away, or sleeping
          - whether it is dark outside or the light level is low
          - whether the same alarm has already happened recently

      - type: markdown
        title: Person detection
        content: |
          ## Person detection

          ### Easy version
          This part is for when Frigate sees a person.
          It can send you a warning and make the house react.

          Examples:
          - a person is seen at the backyard
          - a person is seen near the entrance
          - a person is seen while you are away

          ### More advanced version
          The automations use a trigger based on the binary sensor for person activity.
          Then they check the home mode:
          - Sleep mode: alerts are sent quickly
          - Away mode: some alerts are immediate, and some are delayed
          - Home mode: fewer alerts are sent

          The logic also checks which cameras detected the event.
          Some cameras are treated as higher priority, especially the backside cameras.

          This is why you might see:
          - immediate notifications for priority cameras
          - delayed notifications for other cameras
          - blinking lights when a person is detected

      - type: markdown
        title: Animal detection
        content: |
          ## Animal detection

          ### Easy version
          This part is for animals such as cats, dogs, or other wildlife.
          It helps the house react when something animal-like appears.

          Examples:
          - a cat is seen in the backyard
          - a dog appears near the rear yard
          - an animal is detected when it is dark

          ### More advanced version
          The animal logic watches a summary sensor for animal activity on the backside.
          When the sensor turns on, the system checks if it is night or if the light level is low.
          If that is true, the house can:
          - turn on the deck light
          - turn on outdoor floodlights
          - turn them off again after a short time if the detection is gone

          This is why the response is more careful than a simple “lights on” rule.
          It waits a little to avoid reacting to a short flicker.

      - type: markdown
        title: Intruder alarm logic
        content: |
          ## Intruder alarm logic

          ### Easy version
          This is the stronger security part.
          If a person is detected in a sensitive zone, the house can make a more serious response.

          Examples:
          - a person is seen in the backyard zone at night
          - the system decides it is important enough to react strongly
          - a siren is activated briefly
          - a phone notification is sent

          ### More advanced version
          This part listens to Frigate event messages from MQTT.
          It checks:
          - the event type is new
          - the camera is one of the relevant cameras
          - the label is person
          - the event is in the “Baksidan” zone
          - the home mode is Sleep or Away at the right time
          - the alarm has not already fired too recently

          If all conditions are met, the automation:
          - turns the siren on
          - sets the volume to full
          - waits a few seconds
          - turns the siren off again
          - sends a notification with details about the event

      - type: markdown
        title: Face detection
        content: |
          ## Face detection

          ### Easy version
          This part is for face-related events.
          Frigate can publish updates about faces, and Home Assistant can store that information.

          ### More advanced version
          The face part listens to MQTT updates from Frigate.
          It creates sensors for:
          - the detected face name
          - the camera that saw the face
          - the confidence score
          - the timestamp
          - the raw event data

          This is useful if you want to build more advanced automations later.

      - type: markdown
        title: Summary sensors and helpers
        content: |
          ## Summary sensors and helpers

          ### Easy version
          This part makes the system easier to use.
          Instead of having many separate raw values, it creates simple summary sensors.

          Example:
          - “is there any person activity right now?”
          - “is there any animal activity on the backside?”
          - “is there any activity at all?”

          ### More advanced version
          The summary sensors combine values from several camera-specific sensors.
          This means the automations can react to a simple yes/no signal instead of checking many sensors individually.

          That makes the setup cleaner and easier to maintain.

      - type: markdown
        title: Media cleanup
        content: |
          ## Media cleanup

          ### Easy version
          This part helps keep the storage from filling up.
          It can remove old video clips and recordings.

          ### More advanced version
          The cleanup script stops Frigate, removes old media files and database files, and then restarts Frigate.
          This is a maintenance tool, not a normal detection feature.

      - type: markdown
        title: Main files in this group
        content: |
          ## Files behind the Frigate setup

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_person_detected.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_person_detected.yaml)  
            Person detection, alerts, and light reactions.

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_animal_detected.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_animal_detected.yaml)  
            Animal detection and backyard light reactions.

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_intruder_alarm.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_intruder_alarm.yaml)  
            Stronger alarm-style actions for person events.

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_face_detection.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_face_detection.yaml)  
            Face-related MQTT sensors and helpers.

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_sensors.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_sensors.yaml)  
            Summary sensors used by the automations.

          - [packages/frigate/frigate_media.yaml](packages/frigate/frigate_media.yaml)  
            Cleanup of old Frigate media and database files.

      - type: markdown
        title: Final summary
        content: |
          ## Final summary

          Frigate is a smart camera monitoring system.
          In this setup it helps your house react to people, animals, and faces.

          The simple idea is:
          - cameras see things
          - Frigate understands what it sees
          - Home Assistant reacts

          If you want, this page can later be expanded with more groups such as Lights, Climate, Presence, and Media.
